1
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,540
On a night like this, you came into the world.

2
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:31,330
I remember that storm.

3
00:02:31,960 --> 00:02:35,350
All the dogs in King's Landing howled through the night.

4
00:02:35,670 --> 00:02:37,230
I wish I could remember it.

5
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:39,780
I always thought this would be a homecoming.

6
00:02:40,390 --> 00:02:41,860
Doesn't feel like home.

7
00:02:42,290 --> 00:02:44,460
We won't stay on Dragonstone for long.

8
00:02:44,460 --> 00:02:45,270
Good.

9
00:02:47,610 --> 00:02:48,920
Not so many lions.

10
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:51,800
Cersei controls fewer than half the Seven Kingdoms.

11
00:02:51,800 --> 00:02:54,230
The lords of Westeros despise her.

12
00:02:54,230 --> 00:02:57,080
Even before your arrival, they plotted against her.

13
00:02:57,080 --> 00:02:59,700
- Now... - They cry out for their true queen?

14
00:03:00,610 --> 00:03:02,880
They drink secret toasts to my health?

15
00:03:03,490 --> 00:03:05,140
People used to tell my brother that sort of thing,

16
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:07,120
and he was stupid enough to believe them.

17
00:03:12,330 --> 00:03:16,070
If Viserys had three dragons and an army at his back,

18
00:03:16,130 --> 00:03:18,040
he'd have invaded King's Landing already.

19
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:20,520
Conquering Westeros would be easy for you.

20
00:03:20,850 --> 00:03:23,180
But you're not here to be queen of the ashes.

21
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:25,390
No.

22
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:28,060
We can take the Seven Kingdoms

23
00:03:28,060 --> 00:03:30,140
without turning it into a slaughterhouse.

24
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:33,590
If the great houses support your claim against Cersei,

25
00:03:33,590 --> 00:03:34,660
the game is won.

26
00:03:35,740 --> 00:03:37,830
With the Tyrell army and the Dornish on our side,

27
00:03:37,830 --> 00:03:39,720
we have powerful allies in the south.

28
00:03:41,720 --> 00:03:43,500
I never properly thanked you for that.

29
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:46,500
They joined our side, my queen,

30
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,580
because they believe in you.

31
00:03:49,310 --> 00:03:51,570
You served my father, didn't you, Lord Varys?

32
00:03:52,870 --> 00:03:53,760
I did.

33
00:03:53,860 --> 00:03:55,580
And then you served the man who overthrew him.

34
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:56,810
I had a choice, Your Grace--

35
00:03:56,820 --> 00:03:59,260
serve Robert Baratheon or face the headman's axe.

36
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:00,730
But you didn't serve him long.

37
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:02,970
You turned against him.

38
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:07,520
Robert was an improvement on your father, to be sure.

39
00:04:08,250 --> 00:04:12,330
There have been few rulers in history as cruel as the Mad King.

40
00:04:12,330 --> 00:04:14,560
Robert was neither mad nor cruel.

41
00:04:14,940 --> 00:04:17,320
He simply had no interest in being king.

42
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:20,190
So you took it upon yourself to find a better one.

43
00:04:20,610 --> 00:04:21,620
Your Grace,

44
00:04:22,450 --> 00:04:25,340
when I was ready to drink myself into a small coffin,

45
00:04:25,340 --> 00:04:27,250
Lord Varys told me about a queen in the east who--

46
00:04:27,250 --> 00:04:30,410
Before I came to power, you favored my brother.

47
00:04:31,410 --> 00:04:35,180
All your spies, your little birds,

48
00:04:35,320 --> 00:04:38,770
did they tell you Viserys was cruel, stupid, and weak?

49
00:04:40,860 --> 00:04:41,740
Would those qualities have

50
00:04:41,750 --> 00:04:44,880
made for a good king in your learned opinion?

51
00:04:45,370 --> 00:04:47,910
Until your marriage to Khal Drogo, Your Grace,

52
00:04:47,910 --> 00:04:50,370
I knew nothing about you, save your existence

53
00:04:50,370 --> 00:04:52,570
and that you were said to be beautiful.

54
00:04:52,580 --> 00:04:53,760
So you and your friends

55
00:04:53,760 --> 00:04:56,460
traded me like a prized horse to the Dothraki.

56
00:04:56,460 --> 00:04:58,370
Which you turned to your advantage.

57
00:04:58,380 --> 00:04:59,870
Who gave the order to kill me?

58
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:05,470
King Robert.

59
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:08,170
Who hired the assassins?

60
00:05:09,490 --> 00:05:11,020
Who sent word to Essos

61
00:05:11,020 --> 00:05:12,520
to murder Daenerys Targaryen?

62
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:15,790
Your Grace, I did what had to be done to-- -

63
00:05:15,790 --> 00:05:17,040
To keep yourself alive.

64
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:19,270
Lord Varys has proven himself a loyal servant.

65
00:05:19,270 --> 00:05:21,470
Proven himself loyal? Quite the opposite.

66
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:24,830
If he dislikes one monarch, he conspires to crown the next one.

67
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:27,100
What kind of a servant is that?

68
00:05:27,100 --> 00:05:29,320
The kind the realm needs.

69
00:05:29,350 --> 00:05:32,460
Incompetence should not be rewarded with blind loyalty.

70
00:05:32,830 --> 00:05:35,840
As long as I have my eyes, I'll use them.

71
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:39,290
I wasn't born into a great house.

72
00:05:40,230 --> 00:05:41,500
I came from nothing.

73
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:45,260
I was sold as a slave and carved up as an offering.

74
00:05:45,260 --> 00:05:48,790
When I was a child, I lived in alleys, gutters, abandoned houses.

75
00:05:48,790 --> 00:05:51,190
You wish to know where my true loyalties lie?

76
00:05:51,320 --> 00:05:54,600
Not with any king or queen, but with the people.

77
00:05:55,000 --> 00:05:56,930
The people who suffer under despots

78
00:05:56,930 --> 00:05:58,460
and prosper under just rule.

79
00:05:58,460 --> 00:06:00,950
The people whose hearts you aim to win.

80
00:06:03,100 --> 00:06:05,920
If you demand blind allegiance,

81
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:08,250
I respect your wishes.

82
00:06:09,540 --> 00:06:13,080
Grey Worm can behead me or your dragons can devour me.

83
00:06:13,410 --> 00:06:16,010
But if you let me live, I will serve you well.

84
00:06:16,010 --> 00:06:19,160
I will dedicate myself to seeing you on the Iron Throne

85
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:21,190
because I choose you.

86
00:06:21,860 --> 00:06:25,250
Because I know the people have no better chance than you.

87
00:06:34,030 --> 00:06:35,540
Swear this to me, Varys.

88
00:06:37,450 --> 00:06:39,630
If you ever think I'm failing the people,

89
00:06:40,660 --> 00:06:42,730
you won't conspire behind my back.

90
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:45,750
You'll look me in the eye as you have done today,

91
00:06:45,750 --> 00:06:47,730
and you'll tell me how I'm failing them.

92
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:52,130
I swear it, my queen.

93
00:06:59,230 --> 00:07:02,080
And I swear this-- if you ever betray me,

94
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,420
I'll burn you alive.

95
00:07:08,090 --> 00:07:11,430
I would expect nothing less from the Mother of Dragons.

96
00:07:14,750 --> 00:07:15,930
Forgive me, my queen.

97
00:07:16,660 --> 00:07:19,340
A red priestess from As'shai has come to see you.

98
00:07:55,950 --> 00:07:59,070
She once served another who wanted the Iron Throne.

99
00:07:59,670 --> 00:08:02,670
It didn't end well for Stannis Baratheon, did it?

100
00:08:03,570 --> 00:08:05,310
No, it didn't.

101
00:08:05,310 --> 00:08:07,960
You chose an auspicious day to arrive at Dragonstone.

102
00:08:09,110 --> 00:08:13,020
We've just decided to pardon those who once served the wrong king.

103
00:08:17,820 --> 00:08:20,610
The Lord of Light doesn't have many followers in Westeros, does he?

104
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:24,600
Not yet, but even those who don't worship the Lord

105
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:26,080
can serve his cause.

106
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:27,970
What does your lord expect from me?

107
00:08:33,930 --> 00:08:36,140
"The prince who was promised will bring the dawn."

108
00:08:38,010 --> 00:08:39,800
I'm afraid I'm not a prince.

109
00:08:39,810 --> 00:08:41,310
Your Grace, forgive me,

110
00:08:41,310 --> 00:08:43,880
but your translation is not quite accurate.

111
00:08:44,290 --> 00:08:47,320
That noun has no gender in High Valyrian,

112
00:08:47,320 --> 00:08:50,280
so the proper translation for that prophecy would be,

113
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:54,320
"The prince or princess who was promised will bring the dawn."

114
00:08:54,320 --> 00:08:56,560
Doesn't really roll off the tongue, does it?

115
00:08:56,560 --> 00:08:58,070
No, but I like it better.

116
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:01,700
And you believe this prophecy refers to me?

117
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:04,530
Prophecies are dangerous things.

118
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:06,920
I believe you have a role to play.

119
00:09:07,820 --> 00:09:09,060
As does another--

120
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:11,840
the King in the North, Jon Snow.

121
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:14,150
Jon Snow?

122
00:09:14,830 --> 00:09:17,650
- Ned Stark's bastard? - You know him?

123
00:09:18,500 --> 00:09:19,980
I travelled with him to the Wall

124
00:09:19,990 --> 00:09:21,290
when he joined the Night's Watch.

125
00:09:21,290 --> 00:09:24,910
And why do you think the Lord of Light singled out this Jon Snow?

126
00:09:24,910 --> 00:09:27,830
Aside from the visions you've seen in the flames, that is.

127
00:09:27,830 --> 00:09:30,360
As Lord Commander of the Night's Watch,

128
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:32,980
he allowed the wildlings south of the Wall

129
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:34,990
to protect them from grave danger.

130
00:09:35,090 --> 00:09:36,480
As King in the North,

131
00:09:36,480 --> 00:09:39,300
he has united those wildlings with the Northern houses,

132
00:09:39,300 --> 00:09:41,710
so together they may face their common enemy.

133
00:09:41,710 --> 00:09:43,290
He sounds like quite a man.

134
00:09:44,100 --> 00:09:45,600
Summon Jon Snow.

135
00:09:46,260 --> 00:09:47,530
Let him stand before you

136
00:09:47,530 --> 00:09:49,690
and tell you the things that have happened to him,

137
00:09:50,170 --> 00:09:52,520
the things that he has seen with his own eyes.

138
00:09:54,650 --> 00:09:58,680
I can't speak to prophecies or visions in the flames,

139
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:01,280
but I like Jon Snow and I trusted him.

140
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:03,730
And I am an excellent judge of character.

141
00:10:04,990 --> 00:10:06,440
If he does rule the North,

142
00:10:06,470 --> 00:10:08,300
he would make a valuable ally.

143
00:10:09,620 --> 00:10:11,650
The Lannisters executed his father

144
00:10:11,650 --> 00:10:13,740
and conspired to murder his brother.

145
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:17,100
Jon Snow has even more reason to hate Cersei than you do.

146
00:10:21,190 --> 00:10:22,110
Very well.

147
00:10:23,230 --> 00:10:24,580
Send a raven north.

148
00:10:24,950 --> 00:10:28,720
Tell Jon Snow that his queen invites him to come to Dragonstone...

149
00:10:30,060 --> 00:10:31,580
and bend the knee.

150
00:10:41,350 --> 00:10:43,080
Gather round. Come here.

151
00:10:44,540 --> 00:10:46,070
You think it's really Tyrion?

152
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:49,470
It could be someone trying to lure you into a trap.

153
00:10:50,270 --> 00:10:51,580
Read the last bit.

154
00:10:52,420 --> 00:10:55,660
"All dwarves are bastards in their father's eyes."

155
00:10:57,030 --> 00:10:58,070
What does that mean?

156
00:10:58,340 --> 00:11:00,830
It's something he said to me the first night we met.

157
00:11:02,470 --> 00:11:04,460
You know him better than any of us.

158
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:06,750
What do you think?

159
00:11:10,020 --> 00:11:12,210
Tyrion's not like the other Lannisters.

160
00:11:12,720 --> 00:11:15,880
He was always kind to me, but it's too great a risk.

161
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:18,380
"The Seven Kingdoms will bleed

162
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:20,710
as long as Cersei sits on the Iron Throne.

163
00:11:20,710 --> 00:11:21,720
Join us.

164
00:11:21,810 --> 00:11:23,970
Together, we can end her tyranny."

165
00:11:27,790 --> 00:11:29,200
Sounds like a charmer.

166
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:32,300
Of course, the casual mention of a Dothraki horde,

167
00:11:32,300 --> 00:11:34,690
a legion of Unsullied, and three dragons--

168
00:11:35,070 --> 00:11:36,540
a bit less charming.

169
00:11:39,030 --> 00:11:39,810
What?

170
00:11:40,200 --> 00:11:42,500
Fire kills wights, you told me.

171
00:11:42,980 --> 00:11:44,440
What breathes fire?

172
00:11:46,560 --> 00:11:48,490
You're not suggesting Jon meet with her?

173
00:11:48,490 --> 00:11:50,380
- No, too dangerous. - But?

174
00:11:50,980 --> 00:11:53,710
But if the Army of the Dead makes it past the Wall,

175
00:11:54,550 --> 00:11:56,470
do we have enough men to fight them?

176
00:12:00,410 --> 00:12:03,150
If the Mad King's daughter takes the Iron Throne,

177
00:12:03,150 --> 00:12:05,410
she'll destroy the realm as we know it.

178
00:12:06,330 --> 00:12:09,020
Some of you are bannermen of House Tyrell.

179
00:12:09,380 --> 00:12:12,650
But House Tyrell is in open rebellion against the crown.

180
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:15,570
With their help, the Mad King's daughter

181
00:12:15,570 --> 00:12:18,600
has ferried an army of savages to our shores--

182
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:20,600
mindless Unsullied soldiers

183
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:23,350
who will destroy your castles and your holdfasts,

184
00:12:23,350 --> 00:12:27,210
Dothraki heathens who will burn your villages to the ground,

185
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:29,280
rape and enslave your women,

186
00:12:29,280 --> 00:12:32,280
and butcher your children without a second thought.

187
00:12:32,310 --> 00:12:33,870
This is how Olenna Tyrell

188
00:12:33,870 --> 00:12:36,940
rewards centuries of service and loyalty.

189
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:39,840
You all remember the Mad King.

190
00:12:39,990 --> 00:12:43,290
You remember the horrors he inflicted upon his people.

191
00:12:43,350 --> 00:12:45,100
His daughter is no different.

192
00:12:45,100 --> 00:12:48,260
In Essos, her brutality is already legendary.

193
00:12:48,260 --> 00:12:52,320
She crucified hundreds of noblemen in Slaver's Bay.

194
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:54,310
And when she grew bored of that,

195
00:12:55,310 --> 00:12:57,300
she fed them to her dragons.

196
00:12:58,090 --> 00:13:00,960
It is my solemn duty to protect the people, and I will.

197
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:03,080
But I need your help, my lords.

198
00:13:04,310 --> 00:13:06,860
We must stand together, all of us...

199
00:13:08,180 --> 00:13:09,800
if we hope to stop her.

200
00:13:15,540 --> 00:13:18,830
She has three full-grown dragons, Your Grace.

201
00:13:19,970 --> 00:13:23,060
The same as Aegon when he conquered the Seven Kingdoms.

202
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:26,260
How do you propose to stop them?

203
00:13:30,430 --> 00:13:34,400
We are currently at work on a solution, my lord.

204
00:13:41,370 --> 00:13:42,490
Lord Tarly.

205
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:45,000
Ser Jaime.

206
00:13:46,040 --> 00:13:47,760
I believe you know my son.

207
00:13:47,830 --> 00:13:48,830
Ser Jaime.

208
00:13:49,190 --> 00:13:50,530
Rickard, isn't it?

209
00:13:50,670 --> 00:13:51,600
Dickon.

210
00:13:51,750 --> 00:13:52,610
That's it.

211
00:13:53,910 --> 00:13:55,230
Thank you for coming.

212
00:13:55,760 --> 00:13:57,920
The other lords of the Reach look to you for guidance,

213
00:13:57,920 --> 00:13:59,240
now more than ever.

214
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:00,820
They might not have come if you hadn't.

215
00:14:00,820 --> 00:14:03,470
If my queen summons me, I answer the call.

216
00:14:04,710 --> 00:14:07,320
And I've heard what she does to those who defy her.

217
00:14:10,550 --> 00:14:12,040
You ride for Horn Hill today?

218
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:14,450
I have an army to mobilize.

219
00:14:15,340 --> 00:14:17,550
Won't be long before the fighting starts.

220
00:14:17,550 --> 00:14:19,820
And which side will you be fighting for?

221
00:14:21,710 --> 00:14:24,310
You were the only man to defeat Robert Baratheon in battle.

222
00:14:24,310 --> 00:14:25,980
Not even Rhaegar Targaryen could do that.

223
00:14:25,980 --> 00:14:28,120
It's a long ride back to the Reach, Ser Jaime.

224
00:14:28,120 --> 00:14:29,190
How may I serve?

225
00:14:29,190 --> 00:14:32,100
I want you to be my ranking general in the wars to come.

226
00:14:32,140 --> 00:14:34,420
I want you to swear allegiance to Cersei

227
00:14:34,420 --> 00:14:36,890
and I want you to help me destroy her enemies.

228
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:38,530
All her enemies.

229
00:14:39,060 --> 00:14:41,010
Including Olenna Tyrell.

230
00:14:43,810 --> 00:14:45,120
I'm a Tarly.

231
00:14:46,400 --> 00:14:48,140
That name means something.

232
00:14:49,430 --> 00:14:51,900
We're not oathbreakers. We're not schemers.

233
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:54,770
We don't stab our rivals in the back

234
00:14:55,180 --> 00:14:57,510
or cut their throats at weddings.

235
00:14:59,640 --> 00:15:02,370
I swore an oath to House Tyrell.

236
00:15:02,370 --> 00:15:05,060
You swore an oath to the crown as well, Lord Tarly.

237
00:15:07,020 --> 00:15:09,430
I've known Olenna since I was a child.

238
00:15:09,430 --> 00:15:11,640
She was a great woman once.

239
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:13,650
Now she's broken.

240
00:15:14,490 --> 00:15:16,500
She wants revenge so badly,

241
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:18,880
she brought the Dothraki to our shores.

242
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:22,510
The Dothraki in Westeros for the first time in history.

243
00:15:25,460 --> 00:15:27,180
I know you don't like my sister,

244
00:15:27,630 --> 00:15:29,870
but you have to make a choice.

245
00:15:30,530 --> 00:15:32,050
Do you fight with us

246
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:35,370
or with foreign savages and eunuchs?

247
00:15:40,190 --> 00:15:41,560
When the war is won,

248
00:15:42,540 --> 00:15:45,110
the queen will need a new Warden of the South.

249
00:15:45,620 --> 00:15:47,990
I can think of no better man

250
00:15:48,560 --> 00:15:50,200
than Randyll Tarly.

251
00:15:52,410 --> 00:15:54,590
The infection has spread too far.

252
00:15:55,260 --> 00:15:58,210
You should have cut off your arm the moment you were touched.

253
00:16:00,820 --> 00:16:01,840
How long?

254
00:16:04,700 --> 00:16:06,430
It'll be years before it kills you.

255
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:07,560
Could be 10.

256
00:16:08,390 --> 00:16:09,430
Could be 20.

257
00:16:10,050 --> 00:16:11,570
But how long until...?

258
00:16:13,070 --> 00:16:14,170
Your mind?

259
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:18,110
Six months, maybe fewer.

260
00:16:33,420 --> 00:16:35,580
Pardon, Archmaester.

261
00:16:36,830 --> 00:16:39,620
I met Stannis Baratheon's daughter at Castle Black.

262
00:16:39,620 --> 00:16:42,160
She had the greyscale as a baby and was cured.

263
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:43,680
- No. - Isn't there some way--

264
00:16:43,680 --> 00:16:45,370
Does this look like a baby to you?

265
00:16:45,370 --> 00:16:46,830
- No. - Have you studied

266
00:16:46,830 --> 00:16:48,780
the varying rates of greyscale progression

267
00:16:48,780 --> 00:16:50,570
in infants and fully grown men?

268
00:16:52,460 --> 00:16:53,270
No.

269
00:16:55,770 --> 00:16:57,230
Maester Cressen discovered

270
00:16:57,230 --> 00:17:00,280
Shireen Baratheon's affliction immediately.

271
00:17:01,180 --> 00:17:03,150
This is quite advanced.

272
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:07,090
And beyond our skills, ser.

273
00:17:10,630 --> 00:17:13,430
Were you a commoner, I'd have you shipped to Valyria at once

274
00:17:13,430 --> 00:17:15,610
to live out your life with the stone men.

275
00:17:16,150 --> 00:17:19,740
As an anointed knight, I'll allow you one more day.

276
00:17:22,770 --> 00:17:25,450
How you choose to spend that time is up to you.

277
00:17:31,310 --> 00:17:32,420
Come, Samwell.

278
00:17:36,660 --> 00:17:39,190
Should we send word to your family, Ser...?

279
00:17:41,030 --> 00:17:42,060
Jorah.

280
00:17:43,790 --> 00:17:45,230
Jorah Mormont.

281
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:48,120
Mormont?

282
00:17:48,250 --> 00:17:49,610
There's no need.

283
00:17:50,730 --> 00:17:52,690
I've been dead to them for years.

284
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:55,670
Come, Samwell!

285
00:18:09,420 --> 00:18:11,670
Have you ever been down here, Your Grace?

286
00:18:11,870 --> 00:18:13,350
No, I can't say I have.

287
00:18:15,940 --> 00:18:16,960
I haven't seen these since

288
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:19,310
Robert had them removed from the throne room.

289
00:18:19,310 --> 00:18:23,010
Curious that King Robert did not have them destroyed.

290
00:18:23,170 --> 00:18:24,730
They were his trophies.

291
00:18:25,450 --> 00:18:26,300
He couldn't keep them around.

292
00:18:26,300 --> 00:18:27,970
They would have made him look small.

293
00:18:29,130 --> 00:18:31,880
Sometimes he would come down here and look at them.

294
00:18:34,550 --> 00:18:36,980
I believe he brought his whores on occasion.

295
00:18:44,290 --> 00:18:45,970
Balerion the Dread.

296
00:18:48,330 --> 00:18:50,650
The beast that Aegon rode across the sea.

297
00:18:50,830 --> 00:18:52,880
His flames forged the Iron Throne

298
00:18:53,730 --> 00:18:56,120
and brought the Seven Kingdoms to heel.

299
00:18:57,790 --> 00:18:58,850
Powerful...

300
00:19:00,090 --> 00:19:01,540
but not invincible.

301
00:19:05,940 --> 00:19:08,990
Apparently, one of Daenerys's dragons

302
00:19:09,220 --> 00:19:12,850
was wounded by spears in the fighting pits of Meereen.

303
00:19:14,370 --> 00:19:16,060
And if they can be wounded,

304
00:19:16,660 --> 00:19:18,090
they can be killed.

305
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:23,300
The finest artillators and blacksmiths in King's Landing

306
00:19:23,310 --> 00:19:26,190
have been laboring day and night, Your Grace.

307
00:19:32,760 --> 00:19:34,850
If you'll kindly pull that lever.

308
00:19:51,810 --> 00:19:54,420
If you want the Iron Throne, take it.

309
00:19:56,310 --> 00:19:59,610
We have an army, a fleet, and three dragons.

310
00:19:59,610 --> 00:20:01,590
We should hit King's Landing now,

311
00:20:01,590 --> 00:20:03,410
hard, with everything we have.

312
00:20:03,730 --> 00:20:05,560
The city will fall within a day.

313
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:06,680
If we turn the dragons loose,

314
00:20:06,690 --> 00:20:08,420
tens of thousands will die in the firestorms.

315
00:20:08,420 --> 00:20:10,010
It's called war.

316
00:20:10,020 --> 00:20:12,920
You don't have the stomach for it, scurry back into hiding.

317
00:20:12,930 --> 00:20:14,250
I know how you wage war.

318
00:20:14,250 --> 00:20:16,400
We don't poison little girls here.

319
00:20:17,310 --> 00:20:18,240
Myrcella was innocent.

320
00:20:18,240 --> 00:20:19,700
She was a Lannister.

321
00:20:19,700 --> 00:20:21,920
There are no innocent Lannisters.

322
00:20:22,500 --> 00:20:25,560
My greatest regret is that Oberyn died fighting for you.

323
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:26,740
That's enough.

324
00:20:27,580 --> 00:20:28,940
Lord Tyrion is Hand of the Queen.

325
00:20:28,940 --> 00:20:30,910
You will treat him with respect.

326
00:20:34,630 --> 00:20:37,780
I am not here to be queen of the ashes.

327
00:20:38,880 --> 00:20:40,550
That's very nice to hear.

328
00:20:41,040 --> 00:20:42,840
Of course, I can't remember a queen

329
00:20:42,840 --> 00:20:45,510
who was better loved than my granddaughter.

330
00:20:46,050 --> 00:20:47,770
The common people loved her.

331
00:20:47,770 --> 00:20:49,440
The nobles loved her.

332
00:20:49,730 --> 00:20:51,310
And what is left of her now?

333
00:20:51,960 --> 00:20:53,010
Ashes.

334
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:55,760
Commoners, nobles,

335
00:20:55,760 --> 00:20:57,560
they're all just children, really.

336
00:20:57,860 --> 00:21:01,920
They won't obey you unless they fear you.

337
00:21:03,460 --> 00:21:05,590
I'm grateful to you, Lady Olenna, for your counsel.

338
00:21:05,590 --> 00:21:07,050
I'm grateful to all of you.

339
00:21:07,740 --> 00:21:09,860
But you have chosen to follow me.

340
00:21:09,940 --> 00:21:11,970
I will not attack King's Landing.

341
00:21:12,710 --> 00:21:15,800
We will not attack King's Landing.

342
00:21:16,010 --> 00:21:18,680
Then how do you mean to take the Iron Throne?

343
00:21:19,110 --> 00:21:20,780
By asking nicely?

344
00:21:22,550 --> 00:21:23,770
We will lay siege to the capital,

345
00:21:23,770 --> 00:21:26,020
surrounding the city on all sides.

346
00:21:26,070 --> 00:21:27,280
Cersei will have the Iron Throne,

347
00:21:27,280 --> 00:21:29,780
but no food for her army or the people.

348
00:21:29,780 --> 00:21:32,370
But we won't use Dothraki and Unsullied.

349
00:21:32,940 --> 00:21:34,730
Cersei will try to rally the lords of Westeros

350
00:21:34,730 --> 00:21:38,030
by appealing to their loyalty, their love for their country.

351
00:21:38,260 --> 00:21:40,070
If we besiege the city with foreigners,

352
00:21:40,070 --> 00:21:41,350
we prove her point.

353
00:21:41,910 --> 00:21:43,470
Our army should be Westerosi.

354
00:21:43,470 --> 00:21:45,670
And I suppose we're providing the Westerosi?

355
00:21:45,670 --> 00:21:46,680
You are.

356
00:21:47,480 --> 00:21:50,400
Lady Greyjoy will escort you home to Sunspear.

357
00:21:53,360 --> 00:21:55,970
And her Iron Fleet will ferry the Dornish army

358
00:21:55,970 --> 00:21:57,480
back up to King's Landing.

359
00:21:58,900 --> 00:22:01,320
The Dornish will lay siege to the capital

360
00:22:01,500 --> 00:22:03,210
alongside the Tyrell army.

361
00:22:03,210 --> 00:22:05,750
Two great kingdoms united against Cersei.

362
00:22:06,110 --> 00:22:10,700
So, your master plan is to use our armies.

363
00:22:11,370 --> 00:22:14,750
Forgive me for asking, but why did you bother to bring your own?

364
00:22:15,860 --> 00:22:18,430
The Unsullied will have another objective.

365
00:22:18,770 --> 00:22:22,340
For decades, House Lannister has been the true power in Westeros.

366
00:22:22,530 --> 00:22:26,340
And the seat of that power is Casterly Rock.

367
00:22:27,370 --> 00:22:28,560
Grey Worm and the Unsullied

368
00:22:28,560 --> 00:22:31,680
will sail for the Rock and take it.

369
00:22:49,990 --> 00:22:51,320
Do I have your support?

370
00:22:53,410 --> 00:22:54,430
You have mine.

371
00:22:56,690 --> 00:22:58,520
Dorne is with you, Your Grace.

372
00:23:02,700 --> 00:23:03,890
Thank you all.

373
00:23:05,790 --> 00:23:07,750
Lady Olenna, may I speak with you alone?

374
00:23:16,670 --> 00:23:17,550
I realize you're here out

375
00:23:17,550 --> 00:23:20,010
of hatred for Cersei and not love for me.

376
00:23:20,960 --> 00:23:23,530
But I swear to you, she will pay for what she's done.

377
00:23:24,790 --> 00:23:27,770
And we will bring peace back to Westeros.

378
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:28,930
Peace?

379
00:23:29,410 --> 00:23:32,030
Do you think that's what we had under your father?

380
00:23:32,140 --> 00:23:34,340
Or his father? Or his?

381
00:23:35,280 --> 00:23:37,080
Peace never lasts, my dear.

382
00:23:38,080 --> 00:23:40,500
Will you take a bit of advice from an old woman?

383
00:23:42,380 --> 00:23:44,650
He's a clever man, your Hand.

384
00:23:45,020 --> 00:23:47,570
I've known a great many clever men.

385
00:23:48,080 --> 00:23:49,500
I've outlived them all.

386
00:23:49,870 --> 00:23:50,940
You know why?

387
00:23:51,870 --> 00:23:53,190
I ignored them.

388
00:23:54,210 --> 00:23:57,020
The lords of Westeros are sheep.

389
00:23:57,080 --> 00:23:58,490
Are you a sheep?

390
00:23:59,980 --> 00:24:00,940
No.

391
00:24:01,530 --> 00:24:02,750
You're a dragon.

392
00:24:03,910 --> 00:24:05,240
Be a dragon.

393
00:24:09,940 --> 00:24:10,990
Maje.

394
00:24:16,670 --> 00:24:17,990
You leave tomorrow.

395
00:24:21,330 --> 00:24:22,890
Were you going to say goodbye?

396
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:25,590
I will see you when I return.

397
00:24:25,870 --> 00:24:27,560
But you don't know when that will be.

398
00:24:29,770 --> 00:24:30,900
No one knows.

399
00:24:33,650 --> 00:24:35,230
I wish you good fortune.

400
00:24:37,920 --> 00:24:39,130
Missandei.

401
00:24:47,830 --> 00:24:50,310
It is hard for me to say goodbye to you.

402
00:24:50,480 --> 00:24:51,410
Why?

403
00:24:51,910 --> 00:24:52,640
You know why.

404
00:24:52,640 --> 00:24:53,680
I don't.

405
00:24:58,360 --> 00:25:00,660
You are my weakness.

406
00:25:02,030 --> 00:25:03,290
That's what I am?

407
00:25:04,020 --> 00:25:05,340
Your weakness?

408
00:25:05,700 --> 00:25:09,150
When Unsullied are young, the masters learn their fears.

409
00:25:10,670 --> 00:25:12,660
One boy is scared of dogs,

410
00:25:13,470 --> 00:25:15,030
one boy hates high places,

411
00:25:15,040 --> 00:25:17,090
one is frightened of the ocean.

412
00:25:18,050 --> 00:25:20,340
They make the boy sleep with dogs

413
00:25:20,340 --> 00:25:21,670
or climb a cliff.

414
00:25:22,150 --> 00:25:23,660
They throw him in the water.

415
00:25:24,710 --> 00:25:26,770
If he learns to swim, good.

416
00:25:26,880 --> 00:25:28,940
If he drowns, good.

417
00:25:30,090 --> 00:25:32,260
Either way, strong Unsullied.

418
00:25:33,100 --> 00:25:35,400
But I had no fears.

419
00:25:35,490 --> 00:25:39,200
I was never the biggest, never the strongest...

420
00:25:40,930 --> 00:25:44,130
but I was bravest, always.

421
00:25:45,330 --> 00:25:46,850
- I believe it. - Until...

422
00:25:47,350 --> 00:25:51,070
I meet Missandei from the Isle of Naath.

423
00:25:52,670 --> 00:25:55,870
Now I have fear.

424
00:26:01,580 --> 00:26:02,870
I do, too.

425
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:19,620
No.

426
00:27:21,670 --> 00:27:22,960
I want to see you.

427
00:27:24,610 --> 00:27:25,590
Please.

428
00:28:58,900 --> 00:28:59,920
Might be useful.

429
00:28:59,920 --> 00:29:01,400
Ch'Vyalthan was a dreadful writer,

430
00:29:01,400 --> 00:29:03,330
but an excellent researcher.

431
00:29:06,230 --> 00:29:07,700
Maester Faull was quite the opposite,

432
00:29:07,700 --> 00:29:10,710
a brilliant stylist who invented half the stories he tells.

433
00:29:10,710 --> 00:29:12,120
Um, I wanted to ask you...

434
00:29:12,120 --> 00:29:14,360
If you're going to write histories, Tarly,

435
00:29:14,430 --> 00:29:15,630
you have to do the research.

436
00:29:15,640 --> 00:29:17,360
If you want people to read your histories,

437
00:29:17,450 --> 00:29:19,300
you need a bit of style.

438
00:29:19,850 --> 00:29:22,410
I'm not writing "A Chronicle of the Wars Following the Death

439
00:29:22,410 --> 00:29:26,210
of King Robert I" so it can sit on a shelf unread.

440
00:29:28,310 --> 00:29:31,040
What? You don't like the title?

441
00:29:32,010 --> 00:29:33,390
What would you call it, then?

442
00:29:33,400 --> 00:29:36,720
Mm, possibly something a bit more poetic?

443
00:29:37,330 --> 00:29:39,130
We're not poets, Tarly.

444
00:29:39,610 --> 00:29:41,390
Um, Archmaester, if I could just have a moment.

445
00:29:41,390 --> 00:29:42,740
This is your moment.

446
00:29:43,270 --> 00:29:44,570
Use it wisely.

447
00:29:46,900 --> 00:29:49,280
I may have found a way to treat Ser Jorah.

448
00:29:50,900 --> 00:29:51,940
There are two recorded cases

449
00:29:51,940 --> 00:29:54,030
of advanced greyscale being cured.

450
00:29:54,030 --> 00:29:55,780
I found the procedure in the study of rare diseases

451
00:29:55,780 --> 00:29:57,110
by Archmaester Pylos.

452
00:29:57,110 --> 00:29:58,970
I'm familiar with Archmaester Pylos

453
00:29:58,970 --> 00:30:00,940
and his study of rare diseases.

454
00:30:01,440 --> 00:30:02,840
- Oh, you are? - Yes.

455
00:30:03,330 --> 00:30:05,270
And shall I tell you how he died?

456
00:30:06,460 --> 00:30:07,940
From greyscale.

457
00:30:09,530 --> 00:30:11,220
The procedure's far too dangerous,

458
00:30:11,220 --> 00:30:12,940
which is why it's now forbidden.

459
00:30:57,040 --> 00:30:58,020
Hello.

460
00:30:59,090 --> 00:31:00,170
What are you doing?

461
00:31:02,320 --> 00:31:03,600
You're Jorah Mormont,

462
00:31:04,450 --> 00:31:06,380
the only son of Jeor Mormont.

463
00:31:07,810 --> 00:31:09,300
My name is Samwell Tarly,

464
00:31:09,770 --> 00:31:11,560
Sworn Brother of the Night's Watch,

465
00:31:11,560 --> 00:31:13,630
training to serve as maester at Castle Black.

466
00:31:13,990 --> 00:31:15,130
I knew your father.

467
00:31:15,460 --> 00:31:16,830
I was with him when he died.

468
00:31:22,980 --> 00:31:24,960
You are not dying today, Ser Jorah.

469
00:31:31,180 --> 00:31:32,240
Drink this.

470
00:31:32,990 --> 00:31:34,440
- What is it? - Rum.

471
00:31:34,490 --> 00:31:36,770
Drink it all, please. I'm afraid this is going to hurt.

472
00:31:57,230 --> 00:31:59,250
If you could take off your shirt.

473
00:32:13,620 --> 00:32:17,120
If you wouldn't mind, bite down hard.

474
00:32:18,320 --> 00:32:20,080
I'm sorry, but no one knows I'm here,

475
00:32:20,080 --> 00:32:22,670
and if they hear you screaming, then we're both finished.

476
00:32:26,330 --> 00:32:28,020
Have you ever done this before?

477
00:32:35,540 --> 00:32:36,520
No.

478
00:32:37,960 --> 00:32:40,760
But no one else will try it, so I'm the best you've got.

479
00:32:44,290 --> 00:32:45,420
Have a seat.

480
00:32:49,800 --> 00:32:50,560
I'm going to have to remove

481
00:32:50,560 --> 00:32:52,320
the entire upper layer of infected tissue,

482
00:32:52,320 --> 00:32:54,470
then apply a medicinal ointment to the...

483
00:33:12,980 --> 00:33:14,810
Again, I'm sorry,

484
00:33:16,060 --> 00:33:17,900
but please try not to scream.

485
00:34:16,500 --> 00:34:18,940
They say her dragons are bigger than Aegon's.

486
00:34:18,940 --> 00:34:21,780
Horseshit. Cersei's just trying to frighten us.

487
00:34:21,780 --> 00:34:23,060
I hope it's true.

488
00:34:23,180 --> 00:34:26,410
If she lays siege to King's Landing, prices will triple.

489
00:34:26,410 --> 00:34:29,080
As long as we get back there before they start.

490
00:34:29,880 --> 00:34:32,140
One more round. It's a long ride.

491
00:34:33,510 --> 00:34:34,420
Arry!

492
00:34:35,960 --> 00:34:37,090
Hello, Hot Pie.

493
00:34:38,300 --> 00:34:39,310
Sit down.

494
00:34:41,660 --> 00:34:42,680
Who's that for?

495
00:34:51,870 --> 00:34:53,990
Mm. This is good.

496
00:34:55,380 --> 00:34:56,300
You think so?

497
00:34:56,990 --> 00:34:59,570
The secret is browning the butter before making the dough.

498
00:35:00,210 --> 00:35:02,490
Most people don't do that 'cause it takes up too much time.

499
00:35:02,490 --> 00:35:04,270
Mm, I didn't do that.

500
00:35:04,790 --> 00:35:06,030
You've been making pies?

501
00:35:06,540 --> 00:35:07,500
One or two.

502
00:35:08,340 --> 00:35:09,710
I can't believe you're here.

503
00:35:10,190 --> 00:35:11,370
Did you meet the big lady?

504
00:35:12,590 --> 00:35:15,460
- Big lady? - The lady knight?

505
00:35:15,890 --> 00:35:17,930
You know, I figured she was a knight 'cause she had armor on.

506
00:35:18,220 --> 00:35:20,360
She was looking for your sister, but I told her about you.

507
00:35:21,890 --> 00:35:22,980
Did she ever find you?

508
00:35:24,740 --> 00:35:25,690
She found me.

509
00:35:31,500 --> 00:35:33,100
What happened to you, Arry?

510
00:35:43,180 --> 00:35:44,350
You got any ale?

511
00:35:59,700 --> 00:36:01,630
- Where you heading? - King's Landing.

512
00:36:01,760 --> 00:36:04,180
- Why? - Heard Cersei's queen now.

513
00:36:04,180 --> 00:36:05,740
Heard she blew up the Great Sept.

514
00:36:05,740 --> 00:36:07,200
That must have been something to see.

515
00:36:07,820 --> 00:36:09,220
Boom.

516
00:36:09,590 --> 00:36:10,910
I can't believe someone would do that.

517
00:36:11,420 --> 00:36:12,800
Cersei would do that.

518
00:36:15,100 --> 00:36:17,150
I thought you'd be heading for Winterfell.

519
00:36:18,160 --> 00:36:19,770
Why would I go there? The Boltons have it.

520
00:36:20,220 --> 00:36:22,390
No, the Boltons are dead.

521
00:36:25,140 --> 00:36:26,090
What?

522
00:36:26,090 --> 00:36:27,850
Jon Snow came down from Castle Black with a wildling army

523
00:36:27,850 --> 00:36:29,830
and won the Battle of the Bastards.

524
00:36:30,050 --> 00:36:31,450
He's King of the North now.

525
00:36:33,150 --> 00:36:34,110
You're lying.

526
00:36:34,310 --> 00:36:35,600
Why would I lie about that?

527
00:36:36,160 --> 00:36:37,450
He's your brother, right?

528
00:36:44,570 --> 00:36:45,720
Thanks for the pie.

529
00:36:46,910 --> 00:36:48,170
Friends don't pay.

530
00:36:49,240 --> 00:36:50,710
Can't believe I thought you were a boy.

531
00:36:51,310 --> 00:36:52,310
You're pretty.

532
00:36:54,280 --> 00:36:55,260
Thanks.

533
00:37:01,260 --> 00:37:02,770
Take care of yourself, Hot Pie.

534
00:37:03,860 --> 00:37:05,160
Try not to get killed.

535
00:37:05,530 --> 00:37:06,520
Ah, I won't.

536
00:37:06,680 --> 00:37:07,680
I'm like you, Arry.

537
00:37:08,430 --> 00:37:09,480
I'm a survivor.

538
00:37:14,140 --> 00:37:16,040
200 miles to King's Landing.

539
00:37:17,860 --> 00:37:19,940
One bottle of rum. You think we'll make it?

540
00:37:53,840 --> 00:37:54,780
Come in.

541
00:37:55,530 --> 00:37:58,880
A raven, my king, from the Citadel.

542
00:38:09,310 --> 00:38:12,060
This message was sent to me by Samwell Tarly.

543
00:38:12,060 --> 00:38:14,490
He was my brother at the Night's Watch,

544
00:38:14,850 --> 00:38:18,620
a man I trust as much as anyone in this world.

545
00:38:19,460 --> 00:38:21,730
He's discovered proof that Dragonstone

546
00:38:22,240 --> 00:38:24,990
sits on a mountain of dragonglass.

547
00:38:29,220 --> 00:38:32,950
I received this a few days ago

548
00:38:33,400 --> 00:38:34,810
from Dragonstone.

549
00:38:36,740 --> 00:38:39,080
It was sent to me by Tyrion Lannister.

550
00:38:41,120 --> 00:38:44,730
He is now Hand of the Queen to Daenerys Targaryen.

551
00:38:45,220 --> 00:38:48,370
She intends to take the Iron Throne from Cersei Lannister.

552
00:38:48,370 --> 00:38:50,200
She has a powerful army at her back

553
00:38:50,200 --> 00:38:52,880
and, if this message is to be believed,

554
00:38:54,130 --> 00:38:55,360
three dragons.

555
00:38:57,520 --> 00:39:00,190
Lord Tyrion has invited me to Dragonstone

556
00:39:00,190 --> 00:39:01,600
to meet with Daenerys.

557
00:39:03,230 --> 00:39:04,660
And I'm going to accept.

558
00:39:05,060 --> 00:39:06,210
Accept?!

559
00:39:08,920 --> 00:39:11,580
We need this dragonglass, my lords!

560
00:39:12,480 --> 00:39:14,240
We know that dragonglass can destroy

561
00:39:14,240 --> 00:39:16,300
both white walkers and their army.

562
00:39:16,300 --> 00:39:19,650
We need to mine it and turn it into weapons.

563
00:39:21,340 --> 00:39:23,600
But more importantly, we need allies!

564
00:39:23,950 --> 00:39:27,280
The Night King's army grows larger by the day.

565
00:39:27,600 --> 00:39:29,620
We can't defeat them on our own.

566
00:39:29,620 --> 00:39:31,150
We don't have the numbers.

567
00:39:31,150 --> 00:39:34,770
Daenerys has her own army and she has dragonfire.

568
00:39:34,770 --> 00:39:38,100
I need to try and persuade her to fight with us.

569
00:39:38,580 --> 00:39:41,520
Ser Davos and I will ride for White Harbor tomorrow,

570
00:39:42,130 --> 00:39:43,410
then sail for Dragonstone.

571
00:39:43,410 --> 00:39:46,250
Have you forgotten what happened to our grandfather?

572
00:39:46,630 --> 00:39:48,730
The Mad King invited him to King's Landing

573
00:39:48,730 --> 00:39:51,190
- and roasted him alive. - I know that.

574
00:39:51,190 --> 00:39:54,290
She is here to reclaim the Iron Throne and the Seven Kingdoms.

575
00:39:54,290 --> 00:39:56,400
The North is one of those seven kingdoms.

576
00:39:56,400 --> 00:39:59,010
This isn't an invitation; it's a trap.

577
00:39:59,010 --> 00:40:02,400
It could be, but I don't believe Tyrion would do that.

578
00:40:02,400 --> 00:40:04,730
You know him. He's a good man.

579
00:40:04,800 --> 00:40:08,440
Your Grace, with respect, I must agree with Lady Sansa.

580
00:40:08,910 --> 00:40:11,500
I remember the Mad King all too well.

581
00:40:11,660 --> 00:40:13,960
A Targaryen cannot be trusted.

582
00:40:14,520 --> 00:40:16,900
- Nor can a Lannister. - Yeah!

583
00:40:16,900 --> 00:40:19,860
Aye. We called your brother king.

584
00:40:20,240 --> 00:40:23,880
And then he rode south and lost his kingdom.

585
00:40:24,670 --> 00:40:26,810
Winter is here, Your Grace.

586
00:40:27,840 --> 00:40:30,600
We need the King in the North in the North.

587
00:40:30,600 --> 00:40:33,230
Aye!

588
00:40:42,590 --> 00:40:44,440
You all crowned me your king.

589
00:40:46,660 --> 00:40:47,910
I never wanted it.

590
00:40:49,180 --> 00:40:50,820
I never asked for it.

591
00:40:52,070 --> 00:40:55,800
But I accepted it because the North is my home.

592
00:40:56,160 --> 00:40:59,790
It's part of me, and I will never stop fighting for it,

593
00:40:59,790 --> 00:41:01,210
no matter the odds.

594
00:41:04,190 --> 00:41:05,870
But the odds are against us.

595
00:41:09,390 --> 00:41:12,430
None of you have seen the Army of the Dead. None of you.

596
00:41:13,350 --> 00:41:16,230
We can never hope to defeat them alone.

597
00:41:16,230 --> 00:41:19,560
We need allies, powerful allies.

598
00:41:22,210 --> 00:41:24,000
I know it's a risk.

599
00:41:25,990 --> 00:41:27,350
But I have to take it.

600
00:41:27,350 --> 00:41:30,160
Then send an emissary. Don't go yourself.

601
00:41:30,160 --> 00:41:31,400
Daenerys is a queen.

602
00:41:31,400 --> 00:41:34,080
Only a king can convince her to help us.

603
00:41:34,890 --> 00:41:35,630
It has to be me.

604
00:41:35,640 --> 00:41:37,700
You're abandoning your people!

605
00:41:37,700 --> 00:41:39,550
You're abandoning your home.

606
00:41:39,550 --> 00:41:41,230
I'm leaving both in good hands.

607
00:41:41,230 --> 00:41:43,060
- Whose? - Yours.

608
00:41:45,240 --> 00:41:46,270
You are my sister.

609
00:41:46,270 --> 00:41:48,420
You're the only Stark in Winterfell.

610
00:41:49,060 --> 00:41:52,560
Until I return, the North is yours.

611
00:42:15,640 --> 00:42:17,740
I delivered his bones myself.

612
00:42:19,290 --> 00:42:20,650
Presented them to Lady Catelyn

613
00:42:20,650 --> 00:42:23,240
as a gesture of goodwill from Tyrion Lannister.

614
00:42:24,520 --> 00:42:26,150
Seems like a lifetime ago.

615
00:42:27,780 --> 00:42:30,550
Do give Lord Tyrion my best when you see him.

616
00:42:33,830 --> 00:42:35,460
I was sorry when he died.

617
00:42:35,720 --> 00:42:37,450
Your father and I had our differences,

618
00:42:37,450 --> 00:42:39,530
but he loved Cat very much.

619
00:42:42,140 --> 00:42:43,190
So did I.

620
00:42:46,010 --> 00:42:47,670
She wasn't fond of you, was she?

621
00:42:50,130 --> 00:42:52,640
Well, it appears she vastly underestimated you.

622
00:42:54,990 --> 00:42:56,120
Your father and brothers are gone,

623
00:42:56,120 --> 00:42:58,390
yet here you stand, King in the North.

624
00:42:59,920 --> 00:43:02,480
Last best hope against the coming storm.

625
00:43:07,450 --> 00:43:09,040
You don't belong down here.

626
00:43:10,610 --> 00:43:11,540
Forgive me.

627
00:43:13,960 --> 00:43:16,680
We haven't ever talked... properly.

628
00:43:17,700 --> 00:43:18,990
I wanted to remedy that.

629
00:43:20,280 --> 00:43:22,100
I have nothing to say to you.

630
00:43:23,760 --> 00:43:25,050
Not even "Thank you"?

631
00:43:26,580 --> 00:43:27,210
If it weren't for me,

632
00:43:27,210 --> 00:43:29,410
you'd have been slaughtered on that battlefield.

633
00:43:30,650 --> 00:43:31,750
You have many enemies, my king,

634
00:43:31,750 --> 00:43:33,670
but I swear to you, I'm not one of them.

635
00:43:36,380 --> 00:43:37,520
I love Sansa,

636
00:43:38,480 --> 00:43:39,630
as I loved her mother.

637
00:43:50,530 --> 00:43:54,160
Touch my sister, and I'll kill you myself.

638
00:44:20,130 --> 00:44:21,360
- Ready? - Ready?

639
00:44:25,340 --> 00:44:26,000
Ready!

640
00:44:30,060 --> 00:44:30,810
Come on.

641
00:44:36,290 --> 00:44:37,000
Come on!

642
00:46:26,500 --> 00:46:27,570
Nymeria?

643
00:46:42,290 --> 00:46:45,730
Nymeria, it's me, Arya.

644
00:46:50,840 --> 00:46:52,240
I'm heading north, girl.

645
00:46:55,560 --> 00:46:57,710
Back to Winterfell. I'm finally going home.

646
00:47:01,630 --> 00:47:02,620
Come with me.

647
00:47:13,060 --> 00:47:14,030
Come with me.

648
00:47:42,670 --> 00:47:43,670
That's not you.

649
00:48:00,290 --> 00:48:02,890
You can't have them all. It's not fair.

650
00:48:03,130 --> 00:48:04,430
I'm oldest.

651
00:48:04,440 --> 00:48:07,000
Mama will want Cersei for herself.

652
00:48:07,000 --> 00:48:08,550
She's not my mama.

653
00:48:08,550 --> 00:48:10,090
You can have Cersei.

654
00:48:10,940 --> 00:48:12,300
I want the Mountain.

655
00:48:13,320 --> 00:48:15,090
The Mountain killed Father.

656
00:48:15,390 --> 00:48:16,920
He'll crush you with one hand.

657
00:48:16,930 --> 00:48:19,530
Father got careless. That's what Mama says.

658
00:48:19,540 --> 00:48:21,900
Will you shut up about Mama?

659
00:48:21,900 --> 00:48:23,720
"Mama, Mama, Mama."

660
00:48:23,720 --> 00:48:27,410
Maybe I'll kill you both before we take King's Landing.

661
00:48:27,410 --> 00:48:29,250
And then I won't have to share.

662
00:48:31,590 --> 00:48:33,090
"Mama!"

663
00:48:34,910 --> 00:48:37,010
How can you drink this piss?

664
00:48:37,360 --> 00:48:38,840
When we reach Sunspear,

665
00:48:38,850 --> 00:48:41,330
I'll treat you to a Dornish red.

666
00:48:41,510 --> 00:48:43,070
The best in the world.

667
00:48:44,210 --> 00:48:45,350
Have you ever been to Dorne?

668
00:48:45,580 --> 00:48:46,580
A few times.

669
00:48:47,450 --> 00:48:48,650
Never stayed long.

670
00:48:49,040 --> 00:48:50,430
A boy in every port?

671
00:48:51,090 --> 00:48:52,950
A boy, a girl.

672
00:48:54,310 --> 00:48:55,600
Depends on the port.

673
00:48:59,060 --> 00:49:00,550
Could we get some more?

674
00:49:02,880 --> 00:49:04,150
I thought it wasn't for you.

675
00:49:04,850 --> 00:49:07,000
I'm developing a taste for it.

676
00:49:08,510 --> 00:49:10,610
- He's not your servant. - It's fine.

677
00:49:12,840 --> 00:49:17,190
So, you're going to be Queen of the Iron Islands.

678
00:49:17,530 --> 00:49:18,910
Once I kill my uncle.

679
00:49:19,310 --> 00:49:20,930
And what will you be, handsome?

680
00:49:21,740 --> 00:49:23,320
Whatever my queen commands.

681
00:49:23,450 --> 00:49:27,200
He'll be my advisor, my protector.

682
00:49:27,200 --> 00:49:28,530
Oh, I see.

683
00:49:29,850 --> 00:49:31,370
Your protector.

684
00:49:32,420 --> 00:49:35,320
So, if someone gets too close to you...

685
00:49:35,640 --> 00:49:36,960
He might have to intervene.

686
00:49:36,960 --> 00:49:38,880
To hold that person back.

687
00:49:38,880 --> 00:49:41,040
Until they've made their intentions known.

688
00:49:45,060 --> 00:49:47,060
Why are you standing all the way over there, then?

689
00:49:48,170 --> 00:49:50,540
A foreign invasion is underway.

690
00:49:50,960 --> 00:49:52,000
Leave him be.

691
00:49:55,470 --> 00:49:57,670
Seems like you don't need a protector.

692
00:50:03,580 --> 00:50:04,400
Stay here.

693
00:50:08,560 --> 00:50:10,400
We're under attack!

694
00:50:32,610 --> 00:50:33,550
Euron.

695
00:51:41,990 --> 00:51:44,610
You mother's below deck. Keep her safe.

696
00:53:40,040 --> 00:53:40,840
Kill us.

697
00:53:41,510 --> 00:53:42,620
Get it over with.

698
00:54:07,730 --> 00:54:09,420
Give your uncle a kiss.

699
00:54:45,900 --> 00:54:47,310
Little Theon!

700
00:55:02,070 --> 00:55:04,980
Ah, come on, you cockless coward.

701
00:55:08,710 --> 00:55:10,050
I have her.

702
00:55:10,720 --> 00:55:12,080
Come and get her.

703
00:58:06,570 --> 00:58:09,130
I was born to rule the Seven Kingdoms.

704
00:58:09,130 --> 00:58:10,290
And I will.

